DevOps Interview Preparation Azure
2–4 Years Experience | Tool 11
Production-Level Cloud for DevOps Engineers

For 2–4 years experience, interviewers expect you to design secure Azure architectures, integrate CI/CD, and troubleshoot production issues, not just create resources from the portal.

🔹 Core Azure Interview Questions (2–4 yrs)

• Why choose Azure in enterprise environments?
• Azure global infrastructure (Regions,
Availability Zones)
• Azure Resource Manager (ARM) — why is it important?
• Resource Group — real-world usage
• Azure VM vs Azure App Service
• VM Scale Sets — use cases
• Azure Load Balancer vs Application Gateway
• Azure Storage account types
• Blob vs File vs Disk storage
• Managed Disks — benefits
• Azure Monitor — metrics & logs

🔹 Azure Networking & Security

• Azure Virtual Network (VNet)
• Subnet design best practices
• Network Security Group (NSG) vs Azure
Firewall
• Public IP vs Private IP
• VPN Gateway vs ExpressRoute
• Azure DNS basics
• Azure Active Directory (Azure AD)
• Azure AD users vs service principals
• Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
• Managed Identity — why it’s important?
• Azure Key Vault — secrets, keys, certificates

🔹 Azure DevOps & CI/CD

• What is Azure DevOps?
• Azure Repos vs GitHub
• Azure Pipelines — YAML vs Classic
• Azure Artifacts
• Azure Boards (basic understanding)
• Azure Pipelines with Docker
• Azure Pipelines with Kubernetes (AKS)
• Azure Container Registry (ACR)
• How do you manage secrets in Azure pipelines?

🔹 Real-World Azure Scenarios

• Azure VM not accessible — troubleshooting steps
• Application slow on Azure — how do you debug?
• Deployment failed in Azure pipeline — what will you check?
• RBAC permission issue — how do you fix it?
• Sudden Azure cost spike — investigation approach
• How do you design high availability in Azure?

💡 Interview Tip:
If you say:
👉 “We use Azure DevOps pipelines, Key Vault, RBAC, and Azure Monitor in production”
you already sound like a strong 2–4 years DevOps engineer.
